1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:06,006
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

2
00:00:06,089 --> 00:00:07,925
THERE IS NO RELATION
TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:11,094
EPISODE 4

4
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:13,889
[alarm beeping]

5
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:17,017
[alarm stops]

6
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,322
How'd I get here?

7
00:00:32,783 --> 00:00:34,409
<i>I'll trust you, Yubin.</i>

8
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:36,578
[in Korean] You can trust me.

9
00:00:37,955 --> 00:00:39,498
[in English] I can trust him, right?

10
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:44,253
[Yubin] Karin! Are you awake?

11
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,381
-Uh… [sighs]
-[Yubin] Breakfast is ready.

12
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:50,300
[sighs]

13
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:53,553
[sighs]

14
00:01:08,277 --> 00:01:09,528
[in Korean] All done.

15
00:01:17,286 --> 00:01:18,370
[in English] Karin.

16
00:01:18,954 --> 00:01:20,080
Why did I hide?

17
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:21,164
Karin?

18
00:01:25,794 --> 00:01:27,546
[stammers, chuckles]

19
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,631
[puffing]

20
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:34,678
-It's early. What are you doing?
-Huh?

21
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:40,225
Um… Nothing. Airing out… [sighing]

22
00:01:40,309 --> 00:01:41,643
[chuckles]

23
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,104
Your breakfast.

24
00:01:45,397 --> 00:01:46,565
Come and eat.

25
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,624
Um… [sighs]

26
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,005
[in Korean] Yesterday.

27
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,299
[in English] Hmm? What about it?

28
00:02:13,008 --> 00:02:14,009
Uh…

29
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,429
Oh, did something happen?

30
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:21,767
[in Korean] You…

31
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,441
snored like crazy.

32
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:32,235
It was so loud.

33
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,862
[in English] I do not snore, okay?

34
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:35,572
[♪ playful music playing]

35
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:38,325
I mean…

36
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:44,873
Maybe a little bit. Not always.
It's just when I'm really tired.

37
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,958
[in Korean] All right.
[in English] Hurry up and eat.

38
00:02:49,378 --> 00:02:50,712
Thanks for the meal.

39
00:02:58,512 --> 00:02:59,763
Hmm?

40
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:00,847
What is this?

41
00:03:01,765 --> 00:03:02,891
I've never had this before.

42
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:05,227
-You like it? Good.
-Mm-hmm.

43
00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:08,522
What you're eating
is a Korean-style toast.

44
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:10,607
Mmm…

45
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:12,776
-It's great!
-[in Korean] Help yourself.

46
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:14,403
There's another one over there.

47
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,947
[in English] Hmm? What about you?

48
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:19,116
[in Korean] I have to go somewhere
real quick.

49
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:20,534
[Karin, in English] Hmm?

50
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,577
Where to? And for how long?

51
00:03:23,328 --> 00:03:24,329
[Yubin chuckles]

52
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:26,039
[in Korean] Boss,

53
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:28,708
you care about me that much?

54
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:29,793
[inhales sharply]

55
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,336
[in English] No, um…

56
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:34,005
I have to keep track
of your hours as your employer and all.

57
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:38,343
[chuckles, speaks Korean]
They're setting up our booth today.

58
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,221
I should go take a look.

59
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:44,099
[sighs]

60
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:45,976
Right…

61
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,188
[in English] I'll be back.

62
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,443
Mmm. Have a good day.

63
00:03:55,152 --> 00:03:56,153
[sighs]

64
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:03,660
"I'll be back…"

65
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:11,418
[sighs]

66
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,586
[in Korean] Sheesh… [sighs]

67
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,505
What the heck was that?

68
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:18,633
How can someone be so cute
so early in the morning?

69
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:22,596
Is she planning on being
so cute all day long?

70
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:26,057
-[phone buzzing]
-Man, hope she didn't hear that.

71
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:30,061
HYEJIN

72
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,314
Hello?

73
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,441
[Hyejin] <i>I got a call from Sia.</i>

74
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,194
Han Sia?

75
00:04:37,277 --> 00:04:40,697
She asked about that land.

76
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:43,366
How does Sia know about my land?

77
00:04:44,034 --> 00:04:47,245
<i>You know her family</i>
<i>is in the resort business.</i>

78
00:04:47,329 --> 00:04:49,706
<i>Sounds like she's interested.</i>

79
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,709
<i>Why don't you meet with her once?</i>

80
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:54,419
Yeah, sure.

81
00:04:54,503 --> 00:04:55,587
When are you coming back?

82
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:57,172
[grunts]

83
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,342
The thing is…

84
00:05:02,219 --> 00:05:03,470
[grunts, sighs]

85
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,972
I need a little time…

86
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,266
You could fly back soon.

87
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:09,893
<i>Want me to book your flight?</i>

88
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:12,604
No, no need. Just…

89
00:05:13,522 --> 00:05:15,857
I'll come back in a few days.

90
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:20,654
This is a huge opportunity.

91
00:05:20,737 --> 00:05:23,490
<i>Don't wait around.</i>

92
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:26,368
I won't. I'm hanging up.

93
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:28,119
[phone beeps]

94
00:05:31,706 --> 00:05:32,749
[sighs]

95
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:48,348
[in English] Mari, hi. I got us something
that'll fix our hangovers!

96
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:49,432
RAMYEON

97
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:51,351
Oh, I'll boil the water then.

98
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:10,287
-So, um… Mari… Can I…
-[Mari] Hmm?

99
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,791
Can I consider today our day one?

100
00:06:15,417 --> 00:06:16,585
Day one of what?

101
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,004
Like, of us becoming official?

102
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,422
Yeah.

103
00:06:20,922 --> 00:06:23,216
Yesterday, did you forget that we…

104
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:26,386
Forget that we what?

105
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,471
[thunderclap]

106
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,517
Wait, don't you remember what we did?

107
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:38,773
-[♪ upbeat music playing]
-[both singing last note]

108
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:40,066
[♪ music ends]

109
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:42,152
[both chuckling, exclaiming]

110
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:45,572
We're doing great!

111
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:47,949
Uh-huh. Thanks to us
and all our hard work,

112
00:06:48,033 --> 00:06:50,327
everyone's gonna line up
for Karin's booth!

113
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:51,745
Thank you for all your training.

114
00:06:51,828 --> 00:06:53,788
[both chuckling]

115
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:56,291
Oh. [gasps]

116
00:06:58,627 --> 00:06:59,878
[gasps]

117
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,591
[sighs]

118
00:07:07,802 --> 00:07:09,346
Wow.

119
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:12,974
Kunam… [gasps]

120
00:07:14,934 --> 00:07:15,935
Uh…

121
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,438
Don't you think that…

122
00:07:19,648 --> 00:07:22,108
this is kind of romantic?

123
00:07:22,651 --> 00:07:24,569
-Huh?
-It's time.

124
00:07:26,071 --> 00:07:27,489
I'm ready for this.

125
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,254
[Kunam] Mari…

126
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:44,714
I really…

127
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:47,717
really like you a lot.

128
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,473
[kettle whistling]

129
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:01,189
[Kunam] Our romantic hug.

130
00:08:01,773 --> 00:08:03,400
-Th-that was…
-Just because we hugged,

131
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,569
it doesn't mean
that we're automatically dating.

132
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:11,324
If it did, I would've been married
over a hundred times by now.

133
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:13,284
[sighs]

134
00:08:14,119 --> 00:08:18,581
We locked eyes romantically.
You felt it too. I know you did.

135
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,669
It wasn't just me, right?

136
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:25,630
[sighs]

137
00:08:25,714 --> 00:08:27,424
I didn't feel anything.

138
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:29,634
Well, other than the alcohol.

139
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:34,097
Well, I… I felt it.

140
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,557
[Mari] Ah, come on.

141
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:37,434
Relax a little.

142
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:39,936
You take everything way too seriously.

143
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:42,939
Want some takuan?

144
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:45,817
I'm taking these.

145
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,864
[door closes]

146
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:52,782
[Mari sighs]

147
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:58,246
[sighs]

148
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:00,832
[in Korean] Bro.

149
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:03,418
Hey…

150
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,632
[both slurping]

151
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,888
[sighs]

152
00:09:14,971 --> 00:09:16,181
Soup sure goes down easy

153
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:19,434
even on a heavy heart.

154
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,395
Being Korean is about consuming food.

155
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:23,605
[sighs]

156
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:24,731
[sighs]

157
00:09:25,982 --> 00:09:28,443
Were you hiding these from me?

158
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:31,321
[grunts] These are Mari's favorites,
so… [chuckles]

159
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:34,449
Selfish guy.

160
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:36,159
Love comes before friendship.

161
00:09:40,163 --> 00:09:42,290
Should we even be thinking about love
in our situation?

162
00:09:42,373 --> 00:09:44,751
I don't know about you,
but I'm going to give it my best.

163
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:47,754
[scoffs] I can't just not go back.

164
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,214
I'll never give up.

165
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:52,926
Anyway, I have stuff to take care of.

166
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,385
[Kunam] You're right.

167
00:09:54,469 --> 00:09:56,387
I have to sort things out

168
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:59,557
and think about
how to show her all my charms.

169
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,560
Good luck.

170
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,438
[sighs]

171
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:27,585
[Karin chuckles]

172
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,506
[in English] There it is.

173
00:10:32,841 --> 00:10:34,300
[chuckles]

174
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:38,054
[chuckles]

175
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,389
Hey, Yubin. Come here.

176
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:41,558
Come look at this! [chuckles]

177
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,184
The sugar levels have finally risen.

178
00:10:43,852 --> 00:10:45,520
-Look at that.
-[in Korean] Let's see.

179
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:47,272
[chuckles]

180
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:49,023
[in English] Well?

181
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:51,234
-[in Korean] Are you that happy?
-So very happy!

182
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,736
-[chuckles] "So very happy"?
-So very happy!

183
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:54,946
[both chuckle]

184
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,281
-"So very happy"?
-Uh-huh.

185
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:58,908
[in English] Also, that strawberry
I've been working on, it bloomed.

186
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:00,076
-Mmm.
-Come look.

187
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,913
Come on! Let's go!

188
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:06,207
-[chuckles]
-[Karin] Hurry up!

189
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,880
-See? Ta-da!
-Ah.

190
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,548
Wow.

191
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:14,799
[chuckles] Aren't they pretty?

192
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:17,260
Mm-hmm.

193
00:11:17,886 --> 00:11:19,345
-Very pretty.
-Mm-hmm.

194
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,640
-They're cute.
-Mm-hmm. I agree.

195
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:28,980
[in Korean] Do these flowers… Ah.

196
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,569
Do these flowers have a meaning too?

197
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,863
[in English] Mm-hmm. Of course.

198
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:39,699
[chuckles] All flowers have meaning.

199
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,784
[In Korean] What is it?

200
00:11:44,746 --> 00:11:46,915
[in English] Love and respect.

201
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:49,584
LOVE AND RESPECT

202
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:50,710
[Yubin] Oh.

203
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:54,881
-Love and respect.
-Respect.

204
00:11:54,964 --> 00:11:56,007
Mm-hmm.

205
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,551
[chuckles] What is it in Korean?

206
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:05,808
[in Korean] Love and respect.

207
00:12:07,143 --> 00:12:09,604
Love and respect.

208
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:12,315
-Yeah. Love and respect.
-Respect.

209
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,650
[chuckles]

210
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:17,654
Love and respect.

211
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:20,782
Love and respect.

212
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,033
-Yes.
-Mmm.

213
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:26,454
Love and respect.

214
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,187
[sighs]

215
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,364
THE SIXTH
GREEN NOVA CORPORATION FESTA

216
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,825
WHERE TOMORROW'S
AGRICULTURE BEGINS

217
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:10,456
SUEYASU FARM

218
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,791
WITH AN AUTHENTIC
ESPRESSO MACHINE

219
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:14,168
-[in English] Good morning.
-Good morning.

220
00:13:14,252 --> 00:13:15,753
MIZUMORI VILLAGE

221
00:13:25,263 --> 00:13:26,264
Good morning.

222
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:29,600
WHERE TOMORROW'S AGRICULTURE BEGINS

223
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:31,477
[chattering]

224
00:13:36,566 --> 00:13:37,567
[seller] Hello there.

225
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,319
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

226
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:42,238
The day's finally here. [sighs]

227
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,615
You've worked hard.

228
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:46,784
-You've worked really hard too, Yubin.
-[grunts]

229
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:51,497
This year, I'll sweep the competition
and get their backing.

230
00:13:52,582 --> 00:13:57,170
And then, Charo Island's products will be
sold all throughout Japan, right?

231
00:13:57,712 --> 00:13:59,797
-[chuckles] That's right.
-[chuckling]

232
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:05,762
This is…

233
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:10,308
CHARO ISLAND
HARVESTING EXPERIENCE

234
00:14:32,205 --> 00:14:34,665
[Yubin chuckles] Uh…

235
00:14:35,792 --> 00:14:37,418
Well, what do you think?

236
00:14:39,170 --> 00:14:40,463
It's amazing.

237
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,219
[grunts]

238
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:49,222
[in Korean] I wanted to recreate
the field you work on

239
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:54,143
and let everyone here see it.

240
00:14:57,313 --> 00:15:00,358
[chuckles, speaks in English]
I think you did a great job.

241
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:02,902
This is just wonderful!

242
00:15:03,653 --> 00:15:04,987
I'm glad.

243
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,281
[chuckles]

244
00:15:07,365 --> 00:15:11,869
[fans squealing, chuckling]

245
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:15,414
Oh. Sleepyhead's island went all out.

246
00:15:15,498 --> 00:15:19,085
-Wow, more than I expected for sure.
-[fans giggling]

247
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:23,047
Too bad you put in all that effort
because you'll be crushed next to me.

248
00:15:23,131 --> 00:15:25,883
-[fans squeal]
-[Reiji] Wanna see it, huh?

249
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:27,927
[fan] Oh, yay!

250
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:30,138
Ta-da!

251
00:15:30,221 --> 00:15:31,931
[fans squealing]

252
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,607
[in Korean] He's the worst.

253
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:44,735
[in English] Word's getting around

254
00:15:44,819 --> 00:15:48,197
you said you're taking home
the win this year, yeah?

255
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,992
Good luck. I mean that, you know?

256
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,660
Like, can't you wait till after?

257
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:54,370
[fans squealing]

258
00:15:54,453 --> 00:15:55,788
Okay, who wants it?

259
00:15:56,622 --> 00:15:59,292
-You can all have one when we're done.
-[fan] Oh, my God, really?

260
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:01,460
[PA system chiming]

261
00:16:01,544 --> 00:16:04,046
[moderator on PA] <i>We want to thank</i>
<i>everyone for your patience.</i>

262
00:16:04,589 --> 00:16:08,926
<i>The Sixth Green Nova Corporation FESTA</i>
<i>is now open to the public.</i>

263
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:10,261
[seller] Thank you.

264
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,805
[moderator] <i>Vote for your favorite</i>
<i>Booth of the Day</i>

265
00:16:12,889 --> 00:16:15,391
<i>on the board in the middle of our venue.</i>

266
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:16,475
<i>We're counting on your vote.</i>

267
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:18,019
IRO ISLAND - CHARO ISLAND
AOBA VILLAGE

268
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:22,023
<i>Thank you for coming, and please enjoy</i>
<i>all that our FESTA has to offer.</i>

269
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:24,817
-[child] Look at these strawberries.
-[Karin] Thank you so much.

270
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:25,902
They're pretty.

271
00:16:25,985 --> 00:16:27,778
-Can I take one?
-Hey, be careful.

272
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:32,533
-Can I have some strawberries?
-Oh. Sure. Thank you.

273
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:33,743
[Yubin] Thank you very much…

274
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:36,370
-Here you are.
-Yay! Yay!

275
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:38,497
[Yubin] Can I show you?
[in Korean] Go like this.

276
00:16:39,874 --> 00:16:40,875
[Karin chuckles]

277
00:16:41,584 --> 00:16:44,629
[in English] Wanna try?
[in Korean] Go like this. [chuckles]

278
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:46,005
[child, in English] Thank you.

279
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,840
[Yubin] Thank you for stopping by.

280
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:49,467
-[visitor] Thank you.
-[Yubin chuckles]

281
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,010
[both chuckle]

282
00:16:52,386 --> 00:16:54,388
[fans clamoring]

283
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:57,058
[fan] Oh, I would love to have
one of those.

284
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,643
-Thanks very much.
-Oh.

285
00:16:58,726 --> 00:16:59,852
[exclaims]

286
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:02,480
-Thank you.
-I'm most excited to be here.

287
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,607
Wow, thank you. Thanks.

288
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:08,069
Wow, thank you. Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you. Thank you.

289
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:10,947
They're going fast.
Thank you. I'm counting on you.

290
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,157
-Yep. Thanks!
-[fan] Oh, wait. Can I get a picture?

291
00:17:13,241 --> 00:17:14,909
[Mari] Karin!

292
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,495
[chuckles]

293
00:17:17,995 --> 00:17:19,622
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

294
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:23,334
Mari.

295
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:27,463
-[Mari] Look who I found! [giggles]
-[chattering]

296
00:17:27,546 --> 00:17:29,757
-[villagers laughing]
-[villager] Karin, over here.

297
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,592
[all] Hi! [laughing]

298
00:17:31,676 --> 00:17:32,802
We made it.

299
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:34,428
[Mari] We're here! [chuckling]

300
00:17:34,512 --> 00:17:36,472
[all exclaiming]

301
00:17:36,556 --> 00:17:38,891
-Hi! Oh!
-[laughing continues]

302
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:43,271
Karin, our booth is
the cutest booth out of everyone's.

303
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:45,898
-[chuckles] Yeah.
-This had to have been so much work.

304
00:17:45,982 --> 00:17:46,983
Not at all.

305
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,527
-[villager] We're all very proud.
-Ah, you're too sweet. Thanks so much.

306
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:53,239
Yubin, thank you for designing
this booth. It's so charming.

307
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,700
-Oh, yes, thank you. Thank you, sir.
-[villagers] Thank you.

308
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,577
Yes, very nice…

309
00:17:57,660 --> 00:18:00,246
Why don't we all take
a group photo together, huh?

310
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:02,039
-Oh, of course.
-That's a great idea.

311
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:03,207
Everybody come here.

312
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:04,959
-Over here.
-Come on.

313
00:18:05,042 --> 00:18:06,043
Come on.

314
00:18:06,127 --> 00:18:08,296
-This way. This way.
-[Karin] Ah…

315
00:18:08,379 --> 00:18:10,298
-Thank you.
-Everybody get in.

316
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:11,632
This way.

317
00:18:11,716 --> 00:18:14,260
-[in Korean] I'm taking the photo!
-[in English] Yes, right here.

318
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:15,928
Yubin, get in it.

319
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:18,306
[in Korean] Yubin, get in here.

320
00:18:19,223 --> 00:18:21,434
-[in English] Yubin. Yubin!
-Come join us!

321
00:18:21,517 --> 00:18:24,812
[all] Come, come! [chuckling]

322
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:27,565
-Hurry, up! Come on!
-Come, come!

323
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:29,233
-Over here.
-Come in, come in!

324
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,318
Right here, right here.

325
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:33,070
-Come on. Right here.
-Come in here, Yubin.

326
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:35,948
Oh! Come on. Come on!

327
00:18:36,032 --> 00:18:38,367
Don't be shy. Come on!

328
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:40,536
[chief] Sorry, but can you take a photo?

329
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,915
I'm a little busy right now but…

330
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:47,418
Ready? Say cheese. Three, two, one…

331
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:50,129
-Nice. Huh?
-Not with you.

332
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:55,885
Don't you know who I am?

333
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:58,095
Are you being serious?
I don't have time for that.

334
00:18:58,179 --> 00:19:00,556
[snarling]

335
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:02,975
[high-pitched whimpering]

336
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:06,145
Oh, yeah, fine. Yeah. I'll do it.
I'll do it. Yeah. Okay, I got it.

337
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,938
Squish together, everybody.

338
00:19:08,022 --> 00:19:09,148
All right, move in.

339
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,691
Little bit tighter together.

340
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:12,860
Closer.

341
00:19:12,943 --> 00:19:15,404
I can't see the people in the back.

342
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:16,781
All right, that's good.

343
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,074
Okay, smile!

344
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,534
Three, two, one… cheese.

345
00:19:21,786 --> 00:19:26,207
[shutter clicking]

346
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:31,504
[♪ upbeat song playing]

347
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:36,050
We have a lot of tasty food here
at our Charo Island booth. [chuckles]

348
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,259
It's delicious.

349
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:38,511
Hi there.

350
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:44,100
It's delicious, right?

351
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:47,103
-Mmm, mmm.
-[in Korean] Are you Korean?

352
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,730
[Kunam] Oh. Why do you ask?

353
00:19:49,814 --> 00:19:51,649
I heard you speaking Korean.

354
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,983
Your Korean is really good.

355
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:55,444
[visitor chuckles] I studied it.

356
00:19:55,528 --> 00:19:57,488
-Your pronunciation's on point.
-[chuckling]

357
00:19:57,571 --> 00:20:01,575
[Kunam] If you don't mind,
please vote for us for Booth of the Day.

358
00:20:01,659 --> 00:20:03,035
[visitor] Okay, we will.

359
00:20:03,119 --> 00:20:04,537
[in English] We appreciate that.

360
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,580
-[in Korean] Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

361
00:20:06,664 --> 00:20:07,873
[in English] Thank you.

362
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,169
What's wrong?

363
00:20:12,253 --> 00:20:13,587
Are you tired?

364
00:20:14,797 --> 00:20:15,798
No.

365
00:20:16,799 --> 00:20:17,925
I'm totally fine.

366
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:24,473
You're popular.

367
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:26,809
Looks like it.

368
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,730
Charo Island's products are perfect.

369
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:32,857
It seems like everyone thinks that.

370
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:37,570
-We welcome you to Charo Island's booth!
-[chuckles]

371
00:20:38,446 --> 00:20:40,740
[both] Try our delicious samples!

372
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:42,908
Sweet potatoes and strawberries!

373
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:44,577
Uh, coming through.

374
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:49,373
[grunts] Here, sweet potatoes!

375
00:20:49,457 --> 00:20:50,583
[Karin] Thank you.

376
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,461
-Wow.
-Wow.

377
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,880
-[in Korean] Here.
-[Kunam] We're back.

378
00:20:55,963 --> 00:20:58,174
-[Karin, Yubin] Ah.
-You should make a round, bro.

379
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:01,594
-Are you sure?
-[Kunam] Yeah, we've got it from here.

380
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:03,721
[in English] There's some time
before the judging starts.

381
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:05,306
You two should take a look around.

382
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:07,558
[sighs] Great idea.

383
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:09,185
[in Korean] Let's go, let's go.

384
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,644
-[in English] Let's go.
-[Karin yelps]

385
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:13,481
All right. I'll leave it to you then.
We'll be back in a minute.

386
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:16,233
-Enjoy! Bye bye.
-Thanks so much! Thank you!

387
00:21:18,194 --> 00:21:19,445
-[Mari] Hmm.
-[Kunam] Hmm.

388
00:21:20,988 --> 00:21:21,989
[sighs]

389
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,407
-[in Korean] Let's go!
-Let's go!

390
00:21:23,908 --> 00:21:26,827
[villagers cheering]

391
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:32,666
-[in English] Let's do our best! Yeah!
-Charo Island!

392
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,585
-[chanting] Charo Island! Charo Island!
-Kumquats!

393
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,921
Kumquats. Our team needs to chant.
Over here.

394
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,131
-Come on, hurry up!
-Charo Island! Charo Island!

395
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:41,717
-Hey, Iro Island! Iro Island!
-[competitors chanting]

396
00:21:41,801 --> 00:21:44,220
-Charo Island!
-[Reiji] Iro Island!

397
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:46,722
-Come on! Louder!
-Iro Island!

398
00:21:46,806 --> 00:21:50,768
-Louder! Iro! Iro!
-Charo Island!

399
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:52,686
[Kunam] Do your best!

400
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:54,980
-Oh, hi, Mr. Iguchi.
-[Mr. Iguchi] Hi, it's been a while.

401
00:21:55,064 --> 00:21:57,316
-I can't believe how long it's been.
-[Mr. Iguchi] How are you?

402
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:59,068
Oh. Ooh!

403
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,736
-Ooh.
-How is it? It's pretty hefty.

404
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:02,071
Chief! How are you?

405
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:03,781
-I haven't seen you in forever.
-Oh, Karin!

406
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,366
-How are things?
-It's so good to see you.

407
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:08,661
-Hi! You remember me?
-Oh! Oh! Karin, hi!

408
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,162
-Everything well, Ms. Koga?
-Mmm, great.

409
00:22:10,246 --> 00:22:12,456
-The tomatoes are so vibrant.
-[Koga] Mmm.

410
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:16,293
[chief] Oh, Karin. Would you like to try
a sample for yourself?

411
00:22:16,377 --> 00:22:18,170
-[Karin] Oh, can I? Thank you.
-[chief] Of course.

412
00:22:18,254 --> 00:22:19,713
-Yubin.
-[Yubin] Huh?

413
00:22:19,797 --> 00:22:20,840
-Tomatoes.
-[chief] Welcome.

414
00:22:20,923 --> 00:22:22,550
-Mmm, good.
-[Yubin] Mmm.

415
00:22:22,633 --> 00:22:25,052
[Koga] Karin. Why don't we get a photo

416
00:22:25,135 --> 00:22:26,428
-since you're here?
-A photo?

417
00:22:26,512 --> 00:22:28,055
-[Yubin, Karin] Pose?
-[chief] Nice.

418
00:22:28,138 --> 00:22:29,682
-[Koga] Something cute.
-Like this.

419
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:31,350
-[chief] Yeah. Say cheese.
-[Koga] Ready?

420
00:22:31,976 --> 00:22:33,185
[camera shutter clicks]

421
00:22:33,269 --> 00:22:34,812
[♪ romantic music playing]

422
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:43,028
Well?

423
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:45,197
-[in Korean] There. Ta-da.
-[in English] All done?

424
00:22:45,281 --> 00:22:46,407
Oh, you're an artist!

425
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:47,616
-Your twin.
-Copy paste.

426
00:22:47,700 --> 00:22:49,201
-We're twins?
-Totally.

427
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:50,578
[both laugh]

428
00:22:50,661 --> 00:22:53,998
-[Karin] It's so cute. [chuckles]
-[Yubin exclaims]

429
00:22:54,874 --> 00:22:57,334
-Oh, wow. [exclaims]
-All right,

430
00:22:57,418 --> 00:22:58,752
-I'm all done.
-[Yubin] Wow.

431
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:00,921
-A heart for you. Thank you.
-Thank you.

432
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,423
Have a good day.

433
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,049
-It's cute. Is that a dog?
-Do you like it?

434
00:23:04,133 --> 00:23:06,051
-Yeah, it is.
-Wow, it's adorable.

435
00:23:06,135 --> 00:23:08,345
-One and two.
-Here.

436
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:12,516
[no audible dialogue]

437
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:22,109
[chuckles, gasps] Look, flowers.

438
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,361
-How pretty.
-Hello.

439
00:23:24,445 --> 00:23:26,363
-Hi there.
-[vendor] Hello.

440
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:39,793
[chuckles]

441
00:23:50,596 --> 00:23:51,597
Let's go.

442
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:59,647
-Cheese.
-[visitors giggling, exclaiming]

443
00:23:59,730 --> 00:24:02,107
Oh, hey. H-H-Hold on, hold on.

444
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:05,444
[visitor] Oh, wow. Hi! Oh!

445
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:08,739
Why are you going over there?
Who the heck does he think he is?

446
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:10,449
-I hate his guts. Huh?
-Excuse me.

447
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:11,909
Can we take a photo together?

448
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:14,203
-[Kunam] So many of you.
-That all right?

449
00:24:14,828 --> 00:24:18,165
-Three, two, one, say, "Cheese."
-[camera shutter clicks]

450
00:24:18,248 --> 00:24:20,000
-Good, thank you.
-It's my pleasure.

451
00:24:20,084 --> 00:24:22,294
[Kunam] Yeah,
that's our social media account.

452
00:24:22,378 --> 00:24:24,213
[visitors clamoring]

453
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,381
Thank you so much.

454
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:26,882
A sample for you.

455
00:24:26,966 --> 00:24:28,175
One for you. Here you are.

456
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:29,677
Thanks for visiting us.

457
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:31,011
-Uh-huh!
-[clamoring continues]

458
00:24:32,221 --> 00:24:34,223
Why's he got that huge grin on his face?

459
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:36,392
Um, could you take a picture of us?

460
00:24:36,934 --> 00:24:39,645
-W-What?
-You should be in the photo. Come on.

461
00:24:39,728 --> 00:24:40,980
[visitor 1 giggles]

462
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:44,191
-I'm really busy.
-[visitor 2] Cheese!

463
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:46,860
[visitor 1] Anyway, uh, okay…

464
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:50,572
-[visitor 3, in Korean] Three, two, one.
-[camera shutter clicks]

465
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:51,949
-[in English] It looks good.
-[sighs]

466
00:24:52,032 --> 00:24:53,534
[visitor 4] Cute. Can I see?

467
00:24:53,617 --> 00:24:55,953
[visitor 5 giggles] You have to take
another one.

468
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,162
[sighs]

469
00:24:57,246 --> 00:24:58,622
[Kunam] Sure.

470
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:08,007
IRO ISLAND - CHARO ISLAND
AOBA VILLAGE

471
00:25:12,845 --> 00:25:14,013
-[child] I see her!
-[sighs]

472
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:16,181
-[children exclaiming]
-[child] She's right here.

473
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:17,933
-[Karin gasps, chuckles]
-We got you a present!

474
00:25:18,017 --> 00:25:20,060
[children exclaiming continues]

475
00:25:20,144 --> 00:25:22,730
What? Thank you!

476
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:25,858
What? What's all this? [chuckles]

477
00:25:25,941 --> 00:25:27,276
You're all so nice.

478
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:29,319
Is your strawberry booth here?

479
00:25:29,403 --> 00:25:30,904
It sure is.

480
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:34,324
-This way or that way?
-[chuckles]

481
00:25:34,408 --> 00:25:35,451
It's over there.

482
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:37,077
-[children exclaiming]
-[Karin] Oh!

483
00:25:37,161 --> 00:25:39,705
-[chuckles]
-[teacher 1] Don't rush.

484
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:42,833
-Thank you.
-[teacher 1] Stay together.

485
00:25:43,459 --> 00:25:44,710
Take your time.

486
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:47,921
[Karin chuckles]

487
00:25:48,005 --> 00:25:49,381
It's been a while.

488
00:25:49,465 --> 00:25:50,549
[gasps]

489
00:25:51,175 --> 00:25:54,344
Yeah, it really has.
It's nice to see you again.

490
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:55,888
What are you doing here?

491
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,473
[teacher 2] He asked us to come.

492
00:25:57,556 --> 00:25:58,557
[chuckles]

493
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:01,435
[chuckles] Yubin…

494
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:06,690
-You got it. Here, you can do it. Here.
-Thank you.

495
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:08,484
-You got this. You can do it.
-[child] Wait!

496
00:26:09,193 --> 00:26:11,570
-[teacher 2] We'll go visit your booth.
-Great, enjoy it.

497
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:14,782
[exclaims, chuckles]

498
00:26:14,865 --> 00:26:16,492
-Here's a present for you.
-Mmm.

499
00:26:17,201 --> 00:26:19,369
-Are you giving me a gift?
-[grunts]

500
00:26:22,331 --> 00:26:26,043
-[in Korean] Thank you. [grunts, chuckles]
-Let's go.

501
00:26:28,629 --> 00:26:32,633
[in English] Excuse me. Sorry.
