502
00:26:32,716 --> 00:26:35,010
-[teacher 1] Did you find one? [chuckles]
-[children clamoring]

503
00:26:35,094 --> 00:26:36,512
Excuse me.

504
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:37,930
Everybody.

505
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,015
Excuse me. Sorry.

506
00:26:40,099 --> 00:26:42,559
-I brought strawberries for all of you.
-[Yubin] Thank you. Behind you.

507
00:26:42,643 --> 00:26:45,020
-[child 1] These are so yummy.
-[child 2] Can we eat it? Really?

508
00:26:45,104 --> 00:26:46,271
Of course you can. Here.

509
00:26:46,355 --> 00:26:48,857
-There's enough for everyone, all right?
-Can we really have one?

510
00:26:48,941 --> 00:26:51,485
-[Karin] Did anybody not get a strawberry?
-[in Korean] My goodness.

511
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:54,404
-[in English] Thank you.
-Wait, can I get a big one?

512
00:26:54,488 --> 00:26:57,282
-[groaning]
-[Karin chuckles]

513
00:26:57,366 --> 00:26:59,910
[children clamoring]

514
00:27:02,496 --> 00:27:03,956
Yummy?

515
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:06,250
-[child 6] A weird green thing's on mine.
-[Karin] What?

516
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,001
Did everyone get at least one?

517
00:27:08,085 --> 00:27:10,129
-Yes. Take that one, hurry.
-Where do I put it?

518
00:27:10,212 --> 00:27:11,588
I'm putting mine here.

519
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:13,966
Charo Island!

520
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:15,551
Kabocha incoming!

521
00:27:16,093 --> 00:27:17,553
Almost there!

522
00:27:17,636 --> 00:27:18,804
I'm here!

523
00:27:18,887 --> 00:27:20,264
-Want one?
-This looks great.

524
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:22,641
-[in Korean] Here, here, here.
-[chief, in English] Here, I got it.

525
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:24,560
-[chief] Wow, kabocha pumpkin.
-[Yubin straining]

526
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:25,936
-Yubin! Yubin!
-Yeah. What's up?

527
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:27,062
Sweet potatoes.

528
00:27:27,145 --> 00:27:29,565
-[in Korean] Sweet potatoes.
-Sweet potatoes. [in English] Okay.

529
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,692
[moderator] <i>The Green Nova Corporation</i>
<i>FESTA judges…</i>

530
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:33,735
-…<i>will now begin their round…</i>
-Everyone, please vote for us!

531
00:27:33,819 --> 00:27:35,279
<i>-…visiting and rating each booth…</i>
-Check us out.

532
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:37,573
-<i>…participating in the competition.</i>
-Showtime, everybody.

533
00:27:37,656 --> 00:27:40,868
[moderator] <i>We ask that each booth has</i>
<i>a representative present</i>

534
00:27:40,951 --> 00:27:43,161
<i>to greet and attend to the judges.</i>

535
00:27:43,954 --> 00:27:45,581
KABOCHA PUMPKIN
KARIN'S STRAWBERRIES

536
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:46,665
[Karin] Mm-hmm.

537
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:49,418
-[Yubin, in Korean] All done.
-[in English] Good.

538
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:50,627
-Okay. Yes.
-Okay.

539
00:27:51,962 --> 00:27:55,424
This year's theme is "Oh, so juicy."
Say it with me. Ready?

540
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:57,885
-"Oh, so juicy." That was great.
-[judges] "Oh, so juicy."

541
00:27:57,968 --> 00:27:59,761
[Reiji] I'm sweeping
the competition again.

542
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:01,305
Ain't it incredible?

543
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:06,018
Iro Island's tangerines are the most
delicious in all of Asia. Here…

544
00:28:06,101 --> 00:28:07,102
Want one?

545
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:09,229
-[Reiji] Absolutely. Oh, so juicy!
-[Yubin exclaims]

546
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:11,607
[Reiji] Look at the rind.
See? It peels right off.

547
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:13,442
[Yubin] Mmm.

548
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:14,526
[chuckles]

549
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:18,989
-Juicy?
-Mm-hmm.

550
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:20,324
Mmm. Really good.

551
00:28:20,908 --> 00:28:22,451
[in Korean] There's no way we'd lose.

552
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:23,785
[in English] Don't worry.

553
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:25,662
-Mm-hmm. [chuckles]
-Everything will work out.

554
00:28:25,746 --> 00:28:28,165
[in Korean] Take deep breaths. Come on.

555
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:31,293
-[breathes deeply]
-[breathes deeply, chuckles]

556
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:33,378
[breathing deeply]

557
00:28:35,464 --> 00:28:36,506
[grunts]

558
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:38,133
-[in English] You got this.
-[Karin] Mm-hmm.

559
00:28:38,216 --> 00:28:39,801
-Oh. Oh, here they come.
-Ah, ah!

560
00:28:41,595 --> 00:28:44,222
-It's great to meet you. Hello.
-[judge 1] Oh, the pleasure is mine.

561
00:28:44,306 --> 00:28:45,599
Thank you for stopping by.

562
00:28:47,059 --> 00:28:48,226
Welcome to our booth.

563
00:28:48,310 --> 00:28:49,436
Happy to have you.

564
00:28:49,519 --> 00:28:52,189
-What a pretty color.
-[Karin] Thank you.

565
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:54,066
-Mind if I take one?
-Yes, go right ahead.

566
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:55,901
[judge 2] They look so fresh
and vibrant. Mmm.

567
00:28:56,944 --> 00:29:00,447
I selected the variety most compatible
with the air and soil

568
00:29:00,530 --> 00:29:03,075
of Charo island,
and no green houses were involved.

569
00:29:03,158 --> 00:29:05,369
-Grown in the elements of nature?
-Whoa.

570
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:08,872
Didn't that make it more difficult?

571
00:29:09,706 --> 00:29:12,125
It sure did. It was a lot harder
than I thought. [chuckles]

572
00:29:12,209 --> 00:29:13,585
-[chuckles]
-I admire your honesty.

573
00:29:13,669 --> 00:29:14,711
[Karin chuckles]

574
00:29:14,795 --> 00:29:17,631
Why are you determined
to grow these outdoors?

575
00:29:17,714 --> 00:29:20,842
Well, it's because my grandfather
inspired me.

576
00:29:22,344 --> 00:29:24,930
When I was young, he always said

577
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:27,808
in nature, strawberries ripen
with each season,

578
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:30,185
and the seasons will determine
their taste.

579
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:34,982
Honestly, learning the rhythms
of each season

580
00:29:35,065 --> 00:29:37,275
is a bit difficult
to determine accurately.

581
00:29:37,359 --> 00:29:38,860
It's worth it though.

582
00:29:38,944 --> 00:29:41,321
When strawberries are given
the freedom to grow,

583
00:29:41,405 --> 00:29:43,782
the resulting taste is quite unique.

584
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:47,452
My goal in all this
is to master that rhythm for myself.

585
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:50,372
-It's so good.
-[chuckles]

586
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:51,957
-Thank you, sir.
-[Yubin] Delicious.

587
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,834
They're very delicious, yeah.

588
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:55,794
-[Karin chuckles]
-The best ones.

589
00:29:55,877 --> 00:29:57,713
-[all chuckle]
-"Karin's Strawberries."

590
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:58,839
I hope you consider us.

591
00:29:58,922 --> 00:30:00,841
[person] It's been quite a while, Karin.

592
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:08,348
-[gasps] Oh, wow, it has. [chuckles]
-[person gasps]

593
00:30:08,432 --> 00:30:11,143
Look at you.
Boy, how you've grown. [chuckles]

594
00:30:11,226 --> 00:30:14,062
-[Karin chuckles]
-Not only did you grow up well,

595
00:30:14,146 --> 00:30:15,480
you're a participant today.

596
00:30:15,564 --> 00:30:16,940
It's so nice to see you.

597
00:30:17,566 --> 00:30:20,694
I heard through the grapevine that
you joined the Green Nova Corporation,

598
00:30:20,777 --> 00:30:22,738
but I never imagined
I'd run into you here.

599
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:25,365
Thanks to that, we're able to meet again.

600
00:30:25,449 --> 00:30:27,284
-[chuckles] Ah.
-[chuckles]

601
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:30,871
Oh, please.

602
00:30:33,457 --> 00:30:34,624
[person grunts]

603
00:30:46,053 --> 00:30:47,429
Ah… [chuckles]

604
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:51,683
If you have documents
related to these strawberries,

605
00:30:51,767 --> 00:30:53,602
will you please email then to me
when you can?

606
00:30:53,685 --> 00:30:54,811
[Karin] Of course.

607
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:56,521
I have an information pack all written up,

608
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:58,356
so I'll send it to you
after I wrap up today.

609
00:30:58,440 --> 00:30:59,566
-Thank you.
-Sure.

610
00:30:59,649 --> 00:31:03,737
Well, if anything comes up, reach out.

611
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:07,908
Thank you very much.

612
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:10,327
-It's been a pleasure. [chuckles]
-[Karin] I agree.

613
00:31:11,244 --> 00:31:12,412
[grunts, chuckles]

614
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:18,794
-[Karin sighs]
-[Yubin grunts]

615
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:21,171
-Did I do okay?
-Yes. You did great.

616
00:31:21,254 --> 00:31:22,589
-It was perfect.
-[chuckles]

617
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:25,008
-[sighs] Oh, I was nervous.
-You're amazing. Yeah.

618
00:31:26,343 --> 00:31:29,012
-So, uh, that…
-Mmm.

619
00:31:29,096 --> 00:31:32,599
-…last guy. Who was that? A vendor?
-Hmm? Mmm.

620
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:34,017
Uh…

621
00:31:34,101 --> 00:31:35,393
He's just…

622
00:31:35,477 --> 00:31:36,895
-this man that…
-[Yubin] Mm-hmm?

623
00:31:36,978 --> 00:31:38,271
…used to visit when I was little.

624
00:31:38,355 --> 00:31:40,440
-Uh-huh.
-He would drop by all the time,

625
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:42,943
-and he was always really kind to us.
-Ah.

626
00:31:43,819 --> 00:31:45,612
The strawberries are marvelous.

627
00:31:49,116 --> 00:31:51,076
Is that man competing as well?

628
00:31:51,159 --> 00:31:55,163
Oh, he's probably a friend or booth staff
that she hired.

629
00:31:55,664 --> 00:32:00,043
Let's see if he's registered
on the pre-event application file…

630
00:32:01,670 --> 00:32:03,630
I'm terribly sorry, sir, but I'm afraid

631
00:32:03,713 --> 00:32:06,466
I don't see him listed
as a participating farmer anywhere.

632
00:32:07,425 --> 00:32:10,345
[grunts] This isn't acceptable
in the slightest.

633
00:32:10,428 --> 00:32:13,306
I'm to be informed of all goings-on
at Green Nova events,

634
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,641
-and I wasn't.
-I…

635
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,560
My apologies.

636
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:20,272
I will confirm who he is
and report back immediately.

637
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:26,111
-The similarity is uncanny.
-[Karin] Please try a sample.

638
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:28,488
-Here you go. Thank you.
-Thanks for stopping by. Oh.

639
00:32:28,572 --> 00:32:30,157
Of course, we have plenty left.

640
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:34,744
Ladies and gentlemen, it is now time

641
00:32:34,828 --> 00:32:38,957
to announce the Green Nova Corporation
sixth annual FESTA event winners.

642
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,542
[cheering]

643
00:32:40,625 --> 00:32:44,880
[emcee] The Green Nova Corporation
FESTA's very own handpicked judging panel

644
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:46,840
evaluated all of the products…

645
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,592
[♪ dramatic music playing]

646
00:32:49,426 --> 00:32:51,928
…as well as the booth operations.

647
00:32:56,933 --> 00:33:00,228
Booth of the Day was voted on
by Festa attendees.

648
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:04,983
The region with the highest total number
of points will be crowned the winner.

649
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:10,906
In addition, Green Nova Corporation will
be providing all the support necessary

650
00:33:10,989 --> 00:33:15,035
to distribute the winning region's
products nationwide!

651
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:17,662
Which region will come out on top
this year

652
00:33:17,746 --> 00:33:20,457
and take home the award of a lifetime?

653
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:21,958
[crowd cheering]

654
00:33:24,085 --> 00:33:27,422
First up, product evaluation.

655
00:33:27,505 --> 00:33:31,343
It was a close call,
but the winner of this category is…

656
00:33:33,678 --> 00:33:34,804
Iro Island!

657
00:33:34,888 --> 00:33:38,975
-Yeah! [cheering]
-[cheering]

658
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:44,147
[fans chanting] Reiji, Reiji!

659
00:33:44,231 --> 00:33:45,899
-[sighs]
-[emcee] Things are heating up.

660
00:33:46,399 --> 00:33:47,984
Reiji, Reiji!

661
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:51,613
-Yeah!
<i>-</i>The next category is booth operation.

662
00:33:52,197 --> 00:33:56,201
Various regional groups have created
entertaining booth designs and operations,

663
00:33:56,284 --> 00:33:57,619
charming the guests.

664
00:33:58,203 --> 00:34:00,664
And the booth operations
category winner is…

665
00:34:00,747 --> 00:34:03,124
I got this. Yeah.

666
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:05,335
[♪ competitive music plays]

667
00:34:08,255 --> 00:34:09,589
Charo Island!

668
00:34:09,673 --> 00:34:11,841
[crowd applauding, cheering]

669
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:14,427
[♪ triumphant music playing]

670
00:34:17,264 --> 00:34:22,018
[emcee] Now this, ladies and gentlemen,
is the moment you've all been waiting for.

671
00:34:22,102 --> 00:34:23,395
The highest combined score,

672
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:26,982
including the points from the category
that carries the most weight,

673
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,066
Booth of the Day,

674
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:30,068
will be crowned Festa winner.

675
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:33,989
-Everyone…
-[sighs]

676
00:34:34,823 --> 00:34:36,866
…are you all ready?

677
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,910
The Sixth…

678
00:34:40,745 --> 00:34:44,708
Green Nova Corporation FESTA winner is…

679
00:34:45,292 --> 00:34:47,585
[drum roll]

680
00:34:57,721 --> 00:34:58,805
[drum roll stops]

681
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:00,265
[emcee] Charo Island!

682
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:02,142
[crowd cheering]

683
00:35:03,184 --> 00:35:05,478
[♪ cheerful pop music playing]

684
00:35:10,734 --> 00:35:13,111
-[Mari] Karin!
-Karin!

685
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:15,905
[Mari] Karin! [laughing]

686
00:35:17,574 --> 00:35:22,912
[exclaims, in Korean]
We won! We won this thing!

687
00:35:23,455 --> 00:35:24,956
[emcee, in English]
The award will be presented

688
00:35:25,040 --> 00:35:28,293
by a Green Nova Corporation Festa
representative.

689
00:35:29,002 --> 00:35:32,088
Charo Island's booth representative,
please step forward.

690
00:35:32,172 --> 00:35:33,798
[chuckling, cheering]

691
00:35:40,221 --> 00:35:42,557
-Congratulations.
-Thank you so much.

692
00:35:48,813 --> 00:35:50,732
[crowd cheers]

693
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:57,656
[emcee] We will now hear a few words
from Charo Island's booth representative,

694
00:35:57,739 --> 00:35:59,157
Shirahama Karin.

695
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,492
Take it away.

696
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:07,040
I'm Shirahama Karin,
and I'm representing Charo Island.

697
00:36:07,123 --> 00:36:10,460
I feel incredibly honored
to receive this award.

698
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:12,921
Our strawberries, kabocha,
and sweet potatoes

699
00:36:13,004 --> 00:36:16,257
are grown with love and effort
on Charo Island's soil.

700
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:18,218
And I am so thrilled to be acknowledged.

701
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:20,804
Today's victory means so much,

702
00:36:21,596 --> 00:36:24,015
as this Festa has given us an opportunity

703
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:27,977
for people all over Japan
to enjoy our produce.

704
00:36:28,061 --> 00:36:30,980
This has always been a dream of mine.

705
00:36:32,273 --> 00:36:35,276
Charo Island's residents, myself included,

706
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:37,654
will do our very best.

707
00:36:37,737 --> 00:36:41,366
We'll create products
that will be cherished and enjoyed by all.

708
00:36:42,242 --> 00:36:44,202
Thank you again for this great honor.

709
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:45,787
[crowd cheers]

710
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:49,708
[Mari] Yay, Karin!

711
00:36:55,463 --> 00:36:57,215
-[emcee] Thank you, Ms. Shirahama.
-[Karin] Thank you.

712
00:36:57,298 --> 00:36:59,384
DO YOU KNOW HOW LONG IT'S BEEN?
CALL ME.

713
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:02,762
All right, everyone. This now concludes
the Sixth Green Nova Corporation Festa.

714
00:37:02,846 --> 00:37:05,056
Thank you all for participating
and coming out.

715
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:07,517
-[sighs]
-Please get home safely.

716
00:37:43,052 --> 00:37:44,637
-[villager chuckles]
-Thanks so much, everyone.

717
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:47,015
[all chattering, chuckling]

718
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:48,266
Congratulations!

719
00:37:48,808 --> 00:37:52,520
-[chief] Great work today, everyone.
-[Karin] Nice teamwork!

720
00:37:52,604 --> 00:37:54,647
Hey, check out the trophy we won.

721
00:37:54,731 --> 00:37:56,274
Ah, so wonderful!

722
00:37:56,357 --> 00:37:58,443
-Yay!
-[chief] It's gonna bring us good luck.

723
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:00,111
[villager] Yeah! [chuckling]

724
00:38:00,737 --> 00:38:03,531
[chief] It's only up from here.
Good things are coming.

725
00:38:05,283 --> 00:38:07,869
[♪ pensive music playing]

726
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:13,124
[no audible dialogue]

727
00:38:21,132 --> 00:38:23,009
We're gonna win! [cheers]

728
00:38:28,556 --> 00:38:29,974
-Yubin.
-[Yubin] Yeah.

729
00:38:31,935 --> 00:38:33,561
You worked hard today too.

730
00:38:33,645 --> 00:38:34,646
Ah.

731
00:38:41,778 --> 00:38:44,030
Mmm. It was fun.

732
00:38:44,113 --> 00:38:45,782
Mm-hmm, it really was.

733
00:38:48,576 --> 00:38:51,162
[in Korean] Hey, so apparently,

734
00:38:51,246 --> 00:38:53,373
there's going to be fireworks nearby.

735
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:55,208
[stammers, in English] The big fireworks.

736
00:38:55,291 --> 00:38:56,835
-Ah.
-Mm-hmm.

737
00:38:56,918 --> 00:38:59,712
-[in Korean] You want to see?
-[in English] Uh-huh. Mmm, yeah.

738
00:38:59,796 --> 00:39:01,756
-Let's do it.
-Huh, really?

739
00:39:01,840 --> 00:39:03,591
-[in Korean] Let's go. Yeah.
-Really?

740
00:39:10,056 --> 00:39:13,560
It's so crowded. [chuckles]

741
00:39:16,521 --> 00:39:17,730
Mmm…

742
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:22,819
[in English] Uh, it's a lot… [chuckles]
…Crowded.

743
00:39:25,196 --> 00:39:26,656
-Hey. This way.
-Hmm? Huh?

744
00:39:26,739 --> 00:39:28,157
-Here. Come with me.
-Oh. Wait.

745
00:39:28,241 --> 00:39:29,951
-[stammers] Sorry.
-Sorry.

746
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:32,287
-[in Korean] Where are we going?
-[in English] Over here. This way. Here.

747
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:35,290
-Hurry. Excuse us.
-[in Korean] Wait. Wait.

748
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:38,501
[in English] Wow.

749
00:39:39,002 --> 00:39:41,004
-Here, here…
-Hmm?

750
00:39:41,087 --> 00:39:44,173
-It's nice, it's quiet. Uh-huh.
-Mm-hmm. Right.

751
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:46,467
[chuckles]

752
00:39:47,135 --> 00:39:49,429
[in Korean] Perfect spot for zoning out.

753
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:51,764
-Hmm?
-Huh?

754
00:39:52,724 --> 00:39:54,934
[in English]
"Hit the bruise"? What is that?

755
00:39:55,018 --> 00:39:57,270
-A bruise?
-[in Korean] The translation is incorrect.

756
00:39:58,104 --> 00:40:01,316
"Zoning out" is when…

757
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:05,153
You're just so overwhelmed.

758
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,946
It's like letting your mind go blank

759
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:09,657
when you don't want to
think about anything.

760
00:40:11,451 --> 00:40:12,827
Ah. [chuckles]

761
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:15,872
[in English] Ah. Mmm, I get it.

762
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:19,918
It's important
to have your own special spot,

763
00:40:20,001 --> 00:40:22,879
someplace all to yourself
when you're feeling overwhelmed.

764
00:40:23,504 --> 00:40:25,715
-Do you have somewhere like that?
-Mm-hmm.

765
00:40:27,592 --> 00:40:28,801
[in Korean] For me…

766
00:40:30,470 --> 00:40:32,597
-This place.
-[in English] Wow.

767
00:40:33,514 --> 00:40:35,141
That's nice.

768
00:40:35,224 --> 00:40:36,768
-[in Korean] Isn't it pretty?
-Ooh.

769
00:40:36,851 --> 00:40:40,980
This is where I go
when things get really tough.

770
00:40:41,648 --> 00:40:44,359
If you ever come to Seoul,
I'll take you there.

771
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:47,654
[in English] Mmm, sounds good to me.

772
00:41:06,339 --> 00:41:07,924
In all honesty,

773
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:11,219
I've never been anywhere outside of Japan.

774
00:41:14,389 --> 00:41:16,432
[in Korean] Oh. Seriously?

775
00:41:17,058 --> 00:41:18,059
Mmm.

776
00:41:19,644 --> 00:41:22,397
[in English] There are lots of things
I've never gotten to try

777
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:23,731
because of my condition.

778
00:41:27,527 --> 00:41:29,696
This is my first time doing this,

779
00:41:30,363 --> 00:41:32,573
walking around,
exploring the city with someone.

780
00:41:34,409 --> 00:41:37,620
Truthfully, I'll probably never even
have a boyfriend.

781
00:41:40,373 --> 00:41:41,624
[in Korean] Why not?

782
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:44,836
[in English]
Anytime I get excited my body collapses.

783
00:41:46,087 --> 00:41:47,922
I collapse when my heart pounds too much.

784
00:41:49,716 --> 00:41:52,093
[sighs] Just holding hands can make me…

785
00:42:01,102 --> 00:42:02,562
[in Korean] What else do you want to do?

786
00:42:10,153 --> 00:42:11,487
[in English] Fall in love.

787
00:42:24,292 --> 00:42:25,293
[in Korean] I like you.

788
00:42:46,355 --> 00:42:48,608
[♪ upbeat music playing]

789
00:43:17,095 --> 00:43:19,388
MERRY BERRY LOVE

790
00:43:19,472 --> 00:43:20,473
NEXT EPISODE

791
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:22,391
[Karin] <i>"For Koreans,</i>
<i>there are steps before romance."</i>

792
00:43:22,475 --> 00:43:24,977
<i>What is our relationship, exactly?</i>

793
00:43:25,061 --> 00:43:26,312
[in Korean] Is that you, Yubin?

794
00:43:27,688 --> 00:43:30,441
[Karin, in English] <i>What's the real reason</i>
<i>you came to this island?</i>
